# api/verible.rules — Verible lint rules for BitFlow (api/routes/style.py).
# Verible's defaults follow the lowRISC/Google SystemVerilog style guides; this file
# adjusts them for a browser IDE. One rule per line: -name off, +name on, +name=k:v.

# The sandbox names files design.v / tb.v, so file-name rules would always fire.
-module-filename
-package-filename
# Editor buffers rarely end in a newline; not worth a warning on every file.
-posix-eof

# Off by default in Verible, on here: they catch real bugs or are industry norms.
+signal-name-style
+suspicious-semicolon
+mismatched-labels
+instance-shadowing
+forbid-negative-array-dim
